UnitSwaps::ClSwapCallback
├── when reached through delegatecall
│   └── it should revert with DirectCallRequired
├── when no callback caller is expected
│   └── it should revert with InvalidCallbackCaller for the caller
├── when another caller invokes the callback
│   └── it should revert with InvalidCallbackCaller for the caller
├── when a completed callback is replayed
│   └── it should revert with InvalidCallbackCaller for the caller
└── given the caller is the expected pool
    ├── when neither token delta is positive
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidCallbackDeltas
    ├── when both token deltas are positive
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidCallbackDeltas
    ├── when both token deltas are zero
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidCallbackDeltas
    └── given exactly one token delta is positive
        ├── given unexecuted route pools remain
        │   └── it should settle the invoice by swapping the previous pool to the caller
        └── given no unexecuted route pools remain
            ├── when the amount owed exceeds the encoded maximum
            │   └── it should revert with TooMuchRequested
            └── given the amount owed is within the encoded maximum
                ├── when the payer is invalid
                │   └── it should revert with InvalidPayer
                ├── when the payer is the execution address
                │   └── it should clear authorization and transfer the owed token
                ├── when the execution address owes the native mirror token beyond the batch native
                │   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the token
                ├── when the payer is the execution owner
                │   └── it should clear authorization and pull the owed token
                └── when token one is owed
                    └── it should transfer the encoded input token
